{
  "sourceId": "thinksr",
  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while the image still moves once through encode, window, and decode.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image is first encoded into a dense field before the compact thought process touches it. Windowing prepares that field for repeated DQ-CTM ticks without restarting the whole pipeline. The recurrence returns only to the thought stage, and the tick parameters are shared. After those shared ticks, the decoder produces the super-resolved output.",
