      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into tokens without dropping it.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a feature field named F. The window operator then partitions that same field into X. The source describes a persistent dense carrier, so windowing reorganizes the field rather than replacing it with a compact state.",
